            <ArticleTitle>Acute Abdomen Caused by Brucellar Hepatic Abscess.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4269/ajtmh.15-0089</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Brucellosis, a zoonosis that is common worldwide, is endemic in many countries, primarily those of the Mediterranean region (including Turkey). Human brucellosis is a systemic infection with a wide clinical spectrum. Although hepatic involvement is very common during the course of chronic brucellosis, hepatic abscess is a very rare complication of Brucella spp. infection. We present a case of hepatic abscess caused by Brucella melitensis, which resembled the clinical presentation of surgical acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
